<%# The head of the open notification in the lane: the link to the full view of what the
    lane shows (the ticket's page, the note's; Inbox::LaneKind#full_path, none for an event
    card, whose one link is its own), then the actions on the notification in words ("Als
    gelesen" / "Als ungelesen", "Archivieren"; archived: "Zurück in die Inbox"), the same
    as in the "···" menu of its row (_notification_actions). Archiving keeps
    the lane open here, the row leaves the list, no jump to the next one.
    The buttons share one form (F2: same height, same light edge): neither is
    the main action of the lane.
    Stable id "inbox_pane_status_pills": a state change swaps only this
    small area, never the whole lane (an open reply form would be lost).
    Above the organisations the stream also matches data-notification-id:
    a late answer cannot replace the head of another notification.
    Locals: notification, kind (Inbox::LaneKind). %>
<%# Above the organisations inbox-lane-head carries the page's list state into the
    actions when they leave (their answer redraws the list). %>
<div id="inbox_pane_status_pills" class="inbox-lane-actions" data-notification-id="<%= notification.id %>"
     <%= tag.attributes(data: { controller: 'inbox-lane-head' }) if inbox_above_organisations? %>>
  <% if (full_view = kind.full_path) %>
    <%= link_to full_view, target: '_top', class: 'inbox-lane-actions__open' do %>
      <%= inbox_lane_full_view_label(kind) %>
      <i class="bi bi-box-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
  <%= render 'organisations/notifications/notification_actions',
             notification: notification, button_class: 'inbox-lane-actions__button', icons: true, open: true %>
</div>
